        <mxCell id="c146" value="&lt;i&gt;Columns A to Q of the Supplier Table are hidden, and its other columns are shown in two strips of the same rows. The Table is filtered to EmployeeMatches greater than zero (6 of 110 suppliers; the row numbers are blue). Selected: the first MatchKey, whose formula shows in the bar: the address, a comma, a space and the city, in capitals. The result block below is on the Ex 5.5 worksheet.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="788" width="860" height="64" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
